[No-Interlacing]
author=heavyjam
description=Outputs a progressive 448-line frame instead of an interlaced one, with the display origin halved to match. The game draws all 448 lines every frame from one fixed draw offset and only flags the result as interlaced, so nothing is resampled and the picture does not move; what changes is that PCSX2 stops deinterlacing a frame that never needed one. It switches the disc to NTSC 60Hz output with the same video-mode words as the 60 FPS group, so it pairs with 60 FPS or NTSC Mode and also works on its own. Applied at boot, so restart the game after ticking it.
gsinterlacemode=1
